  "id": "COMPOUND:9386 - PROTEIN:1146",
  "verbalization": "Luprostiol is implicated in the interaction with Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit through a series of molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Luprostiol acts as a target for Muscarinic acetylcholine receptor M2, which in turn is targeted by a complex compound, (1R,13R)-13-hydroxy-16,17-dimethoxy-2,6-dioxapentacyclo[11.8.0.03,11.05,9.014,19]henicosa-3(11),4,7,9,14,16,18-heptaen-12-one. This compound is also a target of Trigohowilol G, which further links to Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit. The integration of these pathways suggests a potential mechanism involving muscarinic receptor activation and subsequent signaling cascades that may influence the structure or function of Dr hemagglutinin. The evidence supports a possible role for Luprostiol in modulating the activity of this structural subunit through a chain of molecular interactions, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
